#: taguette/templates/alt_templates/phun/welcome.html:78
msgid "Is LibreQDA completely free to use?"
msgstr ""

#: taguette/templates/alt_templates/phun/welcome.html:83
msgid ""
"Yes, LibreQDA is completely free and open-source. You can use it for "
"academic research, personal projects, or commercial purposes without any "
"licensing fees."
msgstr ""

#: taguette/templates/alt_templates/phun/welcome.html:91
msgid "Do I need to install any software?"
msgstr ""

#: taguette/templates/alt_templates/phun/welcome.html:96
msgid ""
"This instance of LibreQDA maintained by the <a "
"href=\"https://www.usherbrooke.ca/phun\" target=\"_blank\" "
"rel=\"noopener\">Plateforme en humanités numériques</a> (Université de "
"Sherbrooke) does not require any installation and runs entirely in your "
"browser. However, advanced users with specific needs can install LibreQDA"
" on their machine or deploy a server."
msgstr ""

#: taguette/templates/alt_templates/phun/welcome.html:104
msgid "Where is my data stored?"
msgstr ""

#: taguette/templates/alt_templates/phun/welcome.html:109
msgid ""
"When using this instance of LibreQDA (libreqda.org), your data is stored "
"on a Canadian university server — specifically, a Calcul Québec "
"supercomputer housed at École de technologie supérieure (Montréal). Keep "
"in mind that this may differ if you use a version of LibreQDA hosted by "
"someone else."
msgstr ""

#: taguette/templates/alt_templates/phun/welcome.html:117
msgid "Can I use any browser?"
msgstr ""

#: taguette/templates/alt_templates/phun/welcome.html:122
msgid ""
"Chromium-based browsers are better supported at the time (e.g. Chromium, "
"Brave). Firefox is not fully supported."
msgstr ""

#: taguette/templates/alt_templates/phun/welcome.html:130
msgid "Why is LibreQDA designed to be so minimalistic?"
msgstr ""

#: taguette/templates/alt_templates/phun/welcome.html:135
msgid ""
"If you find that some of your complex use cases aren’t covered, remember "
"that one shoe never fits everyone. You might turn to other tools that fit"
" your methods, or you can get in touch with us at <a "
"href=\"mailto:phun@usherbrooke.ca\" target=\"_blank\" "
"rel=\"noopener\">phun@usherbrooke.ca</a> to discuss personalised "
"solutions for data collection, analysis or visualisation."
msgstr ""

